the new danger will be peace rot, peace rot, as if peace were a harmful and terrible thing to be avoided. In peacetime, soldiers were dressed in feathers and pickle helmets just for show. The wealth of the gilded age was drawing attention to class differences. Americans were becoming vain and materialistic, and a feat now, cried the aging veterans of the Civil War on both sides. they waxed nostalgic about the values that war brought, the camaraderie of being out in the field in the company of other men, away from women. That would do men well these days, veterans thought,
